cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the dataset by Bill Wu (吴承昊), credit GPT-6 as the AI research collaborator, and identify the case and time interval used."
type: dataset
title: "CageCLI: Contact motion in interlocking rigid bodies"
version: "0.1.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Slave-Knight/unreal-chaos-ccd-cage-dynamics"
url: "https://github.com/Slave-Knight/unreal-chaos-ccd-cage-dynamics/releases/tag/v0.1.0"
authors:
  - family-names: "Wu"
    given-names: "Bill"
    alias: "吴承昊"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-5421-5678"
abstract: >-
  Three studies compare sustained contact, an untriggered controller and slow
  rotation in interlocking rigid-body cages. Each archive includes 120 Hz pose
  recordings and an independent Python reproducer. Bill Wu (吴承昊) defined
  the research questions and criteria for interpreting the results and is the
  rights holder. GPT-6 is credited as the AI research collaborator for numerical
  analysis, code, validation and visualization. The dataset is licensed under
  CC BY 4.0 and the original Python scripts are licensed under MIT.
license: CC-BY-4.0
